                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] The good the bad and the ugly [/h1]\n[b] The puzzle, the presentation, the UI\t[/b]\n\n[u] Early verdict[/u]\nIts a similar situation with Alexey's dwice (If anyone even remembers that existing), on which the concept was interesting and mildly fun, but the presentation left a lot to be desired.\n\n[i] SCORE:5/10\t[/i]\n\n[u] MENU\t[/u]\nIn desperate need of a cleansing. \nFirst thing most players search for are the Options.\nSo did i, went straight to Video, expecting resolution options or a full screen toggle. By doing that, i discovered this menu is completely wrong. \nNow im attempting to make sense of it:\n[list]\n    [*][b] Video:\t[/b] It's a Tutorial video, leads you to YT\n    [*][b] Help:\t[/b]  Are the objectives/rules\n    [*][b] About:[/b] Story/lore of the game\n[/list]\nIn addition a few are missing:\n[list]\n    [*]The previously mentioned resolution options\n    [*]A volume modifier, and the option to enable/disable music or SFX, rather than the crude on/off all sound\n[/list]\n\n[u] GAME\t[/u]\nDespite the odd look the game is rather simple to understand, provided you found the rule list from the Menu.\nIt all comes down to searching the board for items, with a path that collects the correct items to use against the correct enemies.\n\n[b] RULES[/b]\nThere are 3 types of Combat and 4 enemy types.\nIn Combat we have:\n[list]\n    [*]Close Range(SWORD): Mutual exchange of attacks, resulting in damage equal to each current HP\n    [*]MANA(WAND): Doesn't leave you open to damage, provided you collect the required mana (DAMAGE: nº wands x 2) \n    [*]SCROLLS(multiple colors):  Do equal damage to the full HP of each respective colored enemy\n[/list]\nCounter attacks work differently: 1-2-3-4 Damage from blue-gree-purple-red enemies respectivily\n\n[u] user interface\t[/u]\nPoorly designed.\nRules cannot be accessed in-game.\nIn some aspects, information should be shown when highlighted, admittedly we are working with small numbers. But it's obviously confusing if you happen to have missed the rules.\n[list]\n    [*]Health and Mana Bar not showing numbers \n    [*]Scrolls not showing info\n    [*]Attack not showing info\n    [*]No indication on how much health a health pack gives, nor the very pertinent information that all packs will be used when stacked.\n[/list]\n\n[u] Bugs/Exploits: [/u]\nOnly works when the enemy was defeated. \nConsuming a health pack after your health reaches 0, tricks the game into a winning situation. To be honest it doesn't make much of a difference, because enemies need to be approached in a specific order.\n\n\n[quote] This review was submitted for [url=http://steamcommunity.com/groups/gaming_until_end]Gaming Until End[/url], through the generous contribution of [url=http://steamcommunity.com/id/HellCowON]HellCow.[/url] [/quote]",
